WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.150
Nicole: So, let’s look at some of the
key organisations that are involved

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.489
in cyber security in the UK today.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:12.420
Let’s first look at the National Cyber
Security Centre also known as the NCSC.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:19.490
The NCSC is an organisation launched
by the government in 2016, set up to

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.650
support the most critical organisations
in the public sector as well as

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.810
industry and the general public.

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:31.040
Their aim is to 'help make the UK the
safest place to live and work online'.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.610
They offer practical guidance and
will respond to any cyber security

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:39.810
incidents they are made aware of, to
minimise the harm that they may cause.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.830
They also work collaboratively with law
enforcement, defence and intelligence and

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.870
security services and overseas partners.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.830
Their website is a source of
information for individuals and

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.310
families to large organisations,
including the self-employed, small,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:01.750
and medium businesses, the public
sector, and cyber professionals.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:09.130
The information they give can range from
advice about what to do with spyware,

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:14.300
like a scam message about a fake parcel
delivery, to how to defend organisations

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.780
against malware and ransomware attacks.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.259
They also have a wealth of information
on all different aspects of cyber

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.869
security and resources and opportunities
for schools and students who are

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.530
interested in cyber security.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.140
For more information and guidance their
website is well worth checking out.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.920
Next let’s look at Government
Communications Headquarters

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.270
also known as GCHQ

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:45.704
GCHQ are the UK's intelligence,
security, and cyber agency and their

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:49.980
'mission is to keep the country
safe in the real world and online'.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.050
They work with the secret intelligence
agencies, police, and the private sector

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.430
and with overseas partners to do this.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.839
They have always been at the
heart of the British intelligence

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.220
and security agencies.

00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:07.750
The NCSC is part of GCHQ and
together they aim to protect the

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.200
UK citizens and business from
global attack, that may impact the

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.430
country's security and prosperity.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.360
For more information on GCHQ
check out their website.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:24.750
The Information Commissioners Office
or ICO is the UK's independent body

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.220
set up to uphold information rights.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.750
It works in the public interest and
promotes openness by public bodies

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.810
and data privacy for individuals.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.880
It shows clear guidelines about
individuals rights regarding

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.199
their data and its use and the
individual’s right to access their

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.620
data or correct it if necessary.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.590
For more information on the
ICO check out their website.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.839
And finally let’s look at the UK
Cyber Security Council who state that

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.159
“The UK Cyber Security Council is
the self-regulatory body, and voice,

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:05.360
for UK cyber security education,
training and skills, with a mandate

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.390
from the UK government to be the focal
point through which industry and the

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:14.719
professional landscape advise, shape
and inform national policy on cyber

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:16.160
security professional standards”.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.820
They support the UK Governments National
Cyber Security Strategy to make the UK

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.239
a safe place to live and work online.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.930
They are an umbrella body for
the cyber security profession

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.549
and aim to be a reference point
for cyber security professionals.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.440
For more information on them
check out their website.

